# Seed file for the docker-compose postgrest service's writable config volume (Phase 9,
# scope.md §23 point 7). A one-shot init container copies this into the shared
# `postgrest_config` volume once, the first time it's empty — after that, control-server owns
# the live copy and rewrites its db-schemas line as projects are created
# (ProjectsService/PostgrestConfigService), never this template.
#
# Deliberately the *only* setting here: everything else (db-uri, jwt-secret, etc.) stays as
# PGRST_* environment variables in docker-compose.yml, same as before this file existed — moving
# secrets into a file on a volume control-server can also write to would be a needless expansion
# of what that volume can leak, for no functional benefit (env vars already override file config,
# so mixing the two for exactly one runtime-mutable setting is safe and minimal).
#
# The pre-existing project is listed first, preserving today's no-Accept-Profile-header
# behavior for existing clients (scope.md §23 decision on the default project's legacy naming).
db-schemas = "api"
